  "releaseNotes": "HackerOS 2.2.1, changes for app developers:\n- Mouse Back and Forward buttons in apps. The mouse Back button, Alt+← and the phone's Back (Android button or gesture, iOS swipe) now go to the active app instead of moving the browser tab back and leaving HackerOS; the mouse Forward button and Alt+→ go forward. On a phone, Back follows the ◁ button. Apps receive them through IAppBackHandler and the new IAppForwardHandler, with the new MouseButton and SystemBack sources.\n- App packages carry their satellite assemblies. HackerOsPack puts the satellite assemblies of the app's own assemblies in the package at lib/<culture>/<assembly>.resources.dll; the OS checks them and loads them before the app's first render.\n- HackerOsPack packs every static resource of an app. The package now holds the whole wwwroot/, the collocated .razor.js files and the scoped CSS bundle, declared in the package's manifest with their SHA-256; the publish workflow of the hackeros-solution template copies that manifest into the catalog folder.\n- Signing tool for app authors. dotnet build -t:HackerOsKeyGen creates an author's signing key, HackerOsPack signs each package with the HACKEROS_APP_SIGNING_KEY secret, and the hackeros-solution template publishes the signed packages on the hackeros-packages branch on each version tag. Administrators require an author's signature by adding their public key to [signing-keys].\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/HackerOs/releases/tag/v2.2.1",
